  "failureBoundaries": [
    "Plan left the second daemon with no containers or volumes; an oversized GPU budget failed before allocation.",
    "Controlled interruption retained two partial model shards and the established container. Explicit apply resumed the snapshot and returned an agent reply.",
    "Unchanged apply and export/reapply retained model-file sizes and modification times, container ID and start time. Managed applies still verify an actual agent reply.",
    "Unavailable SSH transport and retargeting the same alias to the original daemon rejected plan and preserved both state files byte-for-byte. Same-named owned fixtures on the original daemon were untouched.",
    "USR1 explicitly tripped the resident protection path after the CLI exited. The container stayed stopped with restart count zero. Explicit apply recovered the same container using unchanged model files.",
    "Native Fabric lifecycle verified external egress denial, actual OpenClaw replies, hosted runtime continuity, model bindings across export/reapply, and managed destroy.",
    "After destroy, a temporary read-only helper verified identical model receipt bytes in the retained volume. The original-engine collision survived managed destroy before explicit fixture cleanup."
  ],
  "discoveries": [
    "Volume verification must use the selected daemon DockerRootDir instead of a client-side /var/lib/docker assumption; fixed in 290ab48394.",
    "ip netns exec hid the cgroup mount for dockerd. The corrected fixture uses nsenter --net to preserve mount visibility.",
    "A separate containerd socket, state and data root are required for this fixture. Containerd 2.2 configuration requires fully qualified disabled-plugin names.",
    "Two distinct daemon identities can refer to the same physical capacity pool; this setup does not prove independent-host capacity observation."
  ],
